# counter harness. One force call is one RgpotCounter.calculate entry.
# Newton and dogleg Hessians are analytic and are not force calls.
# v2 success is under the cap, at the force stop, and Hessian index 0.
# energy and Kabsch RMSD were not applied: the problem file has no energy_tol, rmsd_tol, or per-start reference.
# energy_min and energy_max are the final potential values on the recorded points.
# Default row. gtol and the iteration budget are the problem force norm and the force-call cap. No displacement cap. istep is 0.1. SR2 is Powell's symmetric Broyden update in the SR1 trust region: dogleg when the model is positive definite, otherwise the Cauchy point. With no per-atom cap the trust radius opens at max(istep, 1). There is no line search. The same values are used for every start.
